#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087385 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "9efd33d6-c1d7-55ee-947e-0d067461d5c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-215" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = -6t-3t^2$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t$." :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-6t-3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6-6t \\\\  & =-6(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087386 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle at a Particular Moment Given Its Position"}] :question/id #uuid "136e4bd1-f9c4-50a0-9d16-54709f0d6d45" :question/math-academy-id "e-216" :question/problem "The position $x$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $x(t) = 1+2t+3t^2+4t^3$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t=0$." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $x(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t+3{t}^{2}+4{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =2+6t+12{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+6t+12{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6+24t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=0$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(0) & =6+24(0) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=0$ is $6$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89626065-c358-5daa-bfdb-9e9ad965be20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277241} {:answer/id #uuid "257b3300-0dd0-575a-abf9-ad85c418949b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277242} {:answer/id #uuid "8487d8ae-99df-550e-b1e2-4e961f181430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5e\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277243} {:answer/id #uuid "c4df6798-8140-5760-b202-e3fb228bcd5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277244} {:answer/id #uuid "56bbcfbe-a146-5248-a9ab-6fa3328e0f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8487d8ae-99df-550e-b1e2-4e961f181430" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5e\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277243} :answer-field/id #uuid "634c92dc-28e2-5d94-a251-4d66982ec073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb90cea8-c194-5f3c-8376-493a94dba4ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-102616" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t).$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+4t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1+4 \\\\  & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=6,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =5+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡t & =1 \\\\ {e}^{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)} & ={e}^{1} \\\\ t & =e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=e,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(e) & =(e\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+4e) \\\\  & =e(1)+4e \\\\  & =5e\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=6\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $5e\\text{ m/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088036 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle at a Particular Moment Given Its Position"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840d200a-d118-584c-a572-6e5f2a1ff97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085161} {:answer/id #uuid "95875530-ff29-5bd4-9309-e491e98c0c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085162} {:answer/id #uuid "b740f0a4-8bbf-5b50-882f-4b22454c5d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "98m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085163} {:answer/id #uuid "39053dd3-6857-5055-85a5-1ac0545e38d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085164} {:answer/id #uuid "3c298926-6535-56ad-b2a9-e4d8fdb785ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95875530-ff29-5bd4-9309-e491e98c0c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "92m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085162} :answer-field/id #uuid "14781438-a498-518c-8a1f-0bfa8b648230" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ec6de00-6df9-5919-bfbf-a9df5f1f66a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-2359" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15$, where $t$ is measured in seconds.  Find the particle's acceleration at $t=3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}+10{t}^{2}-15) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}+20t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}+20t) \\\\  & =24t+20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=3$, we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(3) & =24(3)+20 \\\\  & =72+20 \\\\  & =92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration when $t=3$ seconds is $92\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe2c33dc-a25e-5115-821d-2a488578c7c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277248} {:answer/id #uuid "00589345-22ca-5843-9e6f-7da2c12880b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277249} {:answer/id #uuid "374a0e08-4030-591f-b937-d9f89ca1de5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277250} {:answer/id #uuid "9fa23b08-3989-592a-a7ca-6b270f384213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277251} {:answer/id #uuid "a339a6f0-0f50-5a18-a092-07b100d1f732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "374a0e08-4030-591f-b937-d9f89ca1de5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1\\text{ m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277250} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cd1abc5-3394-5abf-95f2-d520b095aff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277247}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b4e7ffe-863b-5593-af94-6129cf7fb536" :question/math-academy-id "q-2361" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=4{t}^{2}-16t+15.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}-16t+15) \\\\  & =8t-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=0,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =8t-16 \\\\ 8t & =16 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=2,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(2) & =4(2)^{2}-16(2)+15 \\\\  & =16-32+15 \\\\  & =-1\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=0\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $-1\\,\\text{m/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0943335-10f4-58f4-a867-9fc0124f9f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0943335-10f4-58f4-a867-9fc0124f9f86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277255} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd921af4-aae4-5aef-a9bc-38b09efbfd86" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fa61f090-9a51-53fc-9eb9-ce631e6c3c5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-315537" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ (in $\\text{m/s}$) of a particle at time $t$ (in seconds) is given by $v(t)=\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}.$ Calculate the velocity of the particle when the acceleration $a$ is equal to $\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nWhen $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ the velocity is $v=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=\\frac{1}{2},$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{2t+1}{2\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2t+1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7}} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7} & =2t+1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+t+7})}^{2} & ={(2t+1)}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}+t+7 & =4{t}^{2}+4t+1 \\\\ 0 & =3{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ 0 & ={t}^{2}+t-2 \\\\ 0 & =(t-1)(t+2) \\\\ t & =1,\\,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $t=1$ since $t\\ge 0.$\n\nThen, to calculate the velocity at time $t=1,$ we substitute this into the equation for the velocity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(1) & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+1+7} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+7} \\\\  & =3\\text{ m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the velocity when $a=\\frac{1}{2}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is $v=3\\,\\text{m/s}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277256 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa3c5cc7-71fb-5010-ad6b-1a533546701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12t^2-4t+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa3c5cc7-71fb-5010-ad6b-1a533546701c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12t^2-4t+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277258} :answer-field/id #uuid "9673dbbd-04cf-5b77-9aaf-b2620c4dcaac" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277257}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a5d4ebd2-81c0-5bff-9a4f-770afd89a880" :question/math-academy-id "q-336411" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+9t.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}+9t) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-4t+9\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0cdcbc5-c10b-5dd1-af9a-410d2d44a4c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c20258f-2a0b-536b-9bad-91fa23c21b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{2}{t^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277261}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c20258f-2a0b-536b-9bad-91fa23c21b8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\frac{2}{t^2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277261} :answer-field/id #uuid "7452ce5f-f87e-5225-8bf5-cca2914bd318" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277260}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5707e23-6e97-5306-b715-e95fd1fbb831" :question/math-academy-id "q-336415" :question/problem "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3{t}^{2}-5t+2}{t}.$ Calculate the acceleration $a$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{3{t}^{2}-5t+2}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-5+\\frac{2}{t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-5+2{t}^{-1}) \\\\  & =3+2(-{t}^{-2}) \\\\  & =3-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277262 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle at a Particular Moment Given Its Position"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e7851bb-80bf-541c-b821-f1c5dd419b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e7851bb-80bf-541c-b821-f1c5dd419b2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277264} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdac6615-f739-5a3d-8a79-8fa482126b15" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "565b31b4-2cd1-5b24-8e88-4ac0f4ecf026" :question/math-academy-id "q-336441" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the time when the particle's acceleration is equal to $a=70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\nThe acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at\n$t=$\n{{field-1}} seconds." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(12{t}^{2}-2t) \\\\  & =24t-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the time when the acceleration is $a=70,$ we substitute this into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}70 & =24t-2 \\\\ 24t & =72 \\\\ t & =3\\text{ }\\text{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the acceleration is $70\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ at $t=3$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277265 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle at a Particular Moment Given Its Position"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04070d84-002d-5243-88f2-eb78a5f072c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277267} {:answer/id #uuid "ecc89e46-066b-54d0-9afe-53af32fb2a90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04070d84-002d-5243-88f2-eb78a5f072c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277267} :answer-field/id #uuid "358ba194-bb39-51d4-a3e6-ee8747dadba5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a67b4607-4f56-5bb6-afe2-1f29e415c471" :question/math-academy-id "q-336448" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=1$ second.\n\n$a(1)=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5{t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =15{t}^{2}-4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(15{t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =30t-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=1$ second, we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =30(1)-4 \\\\  & =26\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle at a Particular Moment Given Its Position"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae4bbbe4-a959-53d8-8d1f-ab71a8b69ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae4bbbe4-a959-53d8-8d1f-ab71a8b69ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277271} :answer-field/id #uuid "eba84d2c-0c78-563a-8459-dfac8d2a5232" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "155a0fbe-b5fe-59e5-9db0-2a3a6209eb2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-336449" :question/problem "The displacement (in meters) of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}+3t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds. Find the particle's acceleration at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ second.\n\n$a(\\frac{1}{2})=$\n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{4}-{t}^{2}+3t) \\\\  & =8{t}^{3}-2t+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8{t}^{3}-2t+3) \\\\  & =24{t}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the acceleration at time $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ second, we substitute $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{1}{2}) & =24{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}-2 \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-2 \\\\  & =4\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe05aa67-e29e-5803-980c-e49ecb5db248" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle at a Particular Moment Given Its Position"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b497b5a7-5305-5068-a36e-5ecc68200ed7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277274} {:answer/id #uuid "5e60107a-c998-5ae7-a420-1edf435880bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e60107a-c998-5ae7-a420-1edf435880bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\cos(2t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277275} :answer-field/id #uuid "598b8183-067e-511b-9b1d-c5b8485396a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "444c1907-febd-59a8-aae6-a4e212ab81e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-336459" :question/problem "The displacement $s$ of a particle moving in a straight line is given by $s(t)=t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t).$ Find the particle's acceleration at time $t.$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $v(t)$ by differentiating $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we differentiate $v(t)$ to find $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
